			label.setBackground(isSelected ? list.getSelectionBackground() : list.getBackground());
			label.setForeground(isSelected ? list.getSelectionForeground() : list.getForeground());
			label.setBorder(BorderFactory.createEmptyBorder(2, 4, 2, 4));
			return label;
		});
		picked.setFixedCellHeight(36);
		for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : initial)
			repaintWhenReady(choice, picked);
		JPanel footer = new JPanel(new BorderLayout(0, 4));
		footer.add(new JScrollPane(picked), BorderLayout.CENTER);
		footer.add(new JLabel("Items in this group — select one or several to remove"), BorderLayout.NORTH);
		JButton remove = new JButton("Remove selected items");
		remove.addActionListener(e ->
		{
			for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : picked.getSelectedValuesList())
				selected.removeElement(choice);
			count();
		});
		picked.getInputMap().put(KeyStroke.getKeyStroke("DELETE"), "remove");
		picked.getActionMap().put("remove", new AbstractAction()
		{
			public void actionPerformed(ActionEvent e)
			{
				remove.doClick();
			}
		});
		JPanel bottom = new JPanel(new GridLayout(0, 1, 0, 4));
		bottom.add(remove);
		bottom.add(hint);
		footer.add(bottom, BorderLayout.SOUTH);
		add(footer, BorderLayout.SOUTH);
		debounce = new javax.swing.Timer(180, e ->
		{
			int version = revision;
			String text = query.getText();
			if (!bankOnly.isSelected() && text.trim().length() < 2)
			{
				hint.setText("Type at least two letters to search all items.");
				return;
			}
			hint.setText("Searching…");
			search.search(text, bankOnly.isSelected() ? bank : null, () -> !closed && revision == version, matches ->
			{
				results.clear();
				for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : matches)
				{
					results.addElement(choice);
					if (choice.image instanceof net.runelite.client.util.AsyncBufferedImage)
						((net.runelite.client.util.AsyncBufferedImage) choice.image)
								.onLoaded(() -> SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() ->
								{
									if (!closed)
										tiles.repaint();
								}));
				}
				hint.setText(matches.size() + " matches shown · " + selected.size() + " selected"
						+ (matches.size() == 80 ? " · refine search" : ""));
			});
		});
		debounce.setRepeats(false);
		query.getDocument().addDocumentListener(new DocumentListener()
		{
			public void insertUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				refresh();
			}

			public void removeUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				refresh();
			}

			public void changedUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				refresh();
			}
		});
		bankOnly.addActionListener(e -> refresh());
		debounce.start();
	}

	private void refresh()
	{
		revision++;
		results.clear();
		debounce.restart();
	}

	private void count()
	{
		hint.setText(selected.size() + " selected" + (limit == 2 ? " (up to two for comparison)" : ""));
	}

	private void addSelected()
	{
		for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : tiles.getSelectedValuesList())
		{
			boolean exists = false;
			for (int i = 0; i < selected.size(); i++)
				if (selected.get(i).id == choice.id)
					exists = true;
			if (!exists && selected.size() < limit)
			{
				selected.addElement(choice);
				repaintWhenReady(choice, picked);
			}
		}
		count();
	}

	int[] ids()
	{
		return Collections.list(selected.elements()).stream().mapToInt(c -> c.id).toArray();
	}

	List<BankItemSearch.Choice> choices()
	{
		return Collections.list(selected.elements());
	}

	private void repaintWhenReady(BankItemSearch.Choice choice, JComponent target)
	{
		if (choice.image instanceof net.runelite.client.util.AsyncBufferedImage)
			((net.runelite.client.util.AsyncBufferedImage) choice.image).onLoaded(() -> SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() ->
			{
				if (!closed)
					target.repaint();
			}));
	}

	void close()
	{
		closed = true;
		revision++;
		debounce.stop();
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.awt.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.List;
import javax.swing.*;
import javax.swing.event.DocumentEvent;
import javax.swing.event.DocumentListener;
import net.runelite.client.util.AsyncBufferedImage;

final class ItemReviewPanel extends JPanel
{
	final JTextField search = new JTextField();
	final DefaultListModel<BankItemSearch.Choice> rows = new DefaultListModel<>();
	final JList<BankItemSearch.Choice> list = new JList<BankItemSearch.Choice>(rows)
	{
		@Override
		public boolean getScrollableTracksViewportWidth()
		{
			return true;
		}
	};
	final JTextArea detail = new JTextArea();
	private final List<BankItemSearch.Choice> choices;
	private final Map<Integer, ItemCatalogueIndex.Rank> reasons;
	private volatile boolean closed;

	ItemReviewPanel(List<BankItemSearch.Choice> choices, Map<Integer, ItemCatalogueIndex.Rank> reasons)
	{
		super(new BorderLayout(0, 8));
		this.choices = new ArrayList<>(choices);
		this.reasons = new HashMap<>(reasons);
		this.choices.sort(Comparator.comparing(c -> c.name));
		JPanel heading = new MarkerForm();
		heading.add(new JLabel(
				"<html>Junk is a review list, not a claim that an item has no use.<br>Amber: a niche or unverified use. Grey: ordinary cleanup review.<br>Sell candidates currently cover reviewed ordinary gathering tools only.</html>"));
		heading.add(new JLabel("Find an item or use"));
		heading.add(search);
		add(heading, BorderLayout.NORTH);
		list.setSelectionMode(ListSelectionModel.SINGLE_SELECTION);
		list.setFixedCellHeight(52);
		list.setCellRenderer((owner, choice, index, selected, focus) ->
		{
			JPanel row = new JPanel(new BorderLayout(8, 0));
			row.setOpaque(true);
			row.setBackground(selected ? owner.getSelectionBackground() : owner.getBackground());
			row.setBorder(BorderFactory.createCompoundBorder(
					BorderFactory.createMatteBorder(0, 3, 0, 0, BankCleanup.colour(reasons.get(choice.id))),
					BorderFactory.createEmptyBorder(4, 5, 4, 4)));
			JLabel icon = new JLabel(choice.image == null ? null : new ImageIcon(choice.image));
			icon.setPreferredSize(new Dimension(36, 32));
			row.add(icon, BorderLayout.WEST);
			JPanel text = new JPanel(new GridLayout(2, 1));
			text.setOpaque(false);
			JLabel name = new JLabel(choice.name), reason = new JLabel(shortReason(choice));
			name.setForeground(selected ? owner.getSelectionForeground() : owner.getForeground());
			reason.setForeground(name.getForeground());
			text.add(name);
			text.add(reason);
			row.add(text, BorderLayout.CENTER);
			row.setToolTipText(shortReason(choice));
			return row;
		});
		detail.setEditable(false);
		detail.setLineWrap(true);
		detail.setWrapStyleWord(true);
		detail.setRows(7);
		detail.setFont(UIManager.getFont("Label.font"));
		detail.setBorder(BorderFactory.createEmptyBorder(8, 8, 8, 8));
		JScrollPane itemScroll = new JScrollPane(list), detailScroll = new JScrollPane(detail);
		itemScroll.setMinimumSize(new Dimension(160, 100));
		detailScroll.setMinimumSize(new Dimension(160, 80));
		JSplitPane split = new JSplitPane(JSplitPane.VERTICAL_SPLIT, itemScroll, detailScroll);
		split.setResizeWeight(0.65);
		split.setBorder(null);
		add(split, BorderLayout.CENTER);
		list.addListSelectionListener(e ->
		{
			if (!e.getValueIsAdjusting())
			{
				BankItemSearch.Choice choice = list.getSelectedValue();
				detail.setText(choice == null ? "Select an item to read its specific uses and evidence."
						: choice.name + " (#" + choice.id + ")\n\n" + reasons.get(choice.id).explanation);
				detail.setCaretPosition(0);
			}
		});
		search.getDocument().addDocumentListener(new DocumentListener()
		{
			public void insertUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				filter();
			}

			public void removeUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				filter();
			}

			public void changedUpdate(DocumentEvent e)
			{
				filter();
			}
		});
		for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : choices)
			if (choice.image instanceof AsyncBufferedImage)
				((AsyncBufferedImage) choice.image).onLoaded(() -> SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() ->
				{
					if (!closed)
						list.repaint();
				}));
		filter();
	}

	private String shortReason(BankItemSearch.Choice choice)
	{
		String[] lines = reasons.get(choice.id).explanation.split("\n");
		return lines.length > 1 && lines[0].equalsIgnoreCase(choice.name) ? lines[1] : lines[0];
	}

	private void filter()
	{
		String query = SearchText.normalize(search.getText());
		rows.clear();
		for (BankItemSearch.Choice choice : choices)
			if (reasons.containsKey(choice.id)
					&& SearchText.normalize(choice.name + " " + reasons.get(choice.id).explanation).contains(query))
				rows.addElement(choice);
		if (!rows.isEmpty())
			list.setSelectedIndex(0);
	}

	void close()
	{
		closed = true;
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.util.*;

final class ItemTaxonomy
{
	private static final Map<String, String> WEAPONS = new HashMap<>();
	private static final Map<String, String> SETS = new HashMap<>();
	static
	{
		for (String[] row : readRows("weapon-roles.tsv", 2))
		{
			WEAPONS.put(row[0], row[1]);
		}
		set("Ahrim — magic set (staff required)", "ahrim's hood", "ahrim's robetop", "ahrim's robeskirt",
				"ahrim's staff");
		set("Dharok — melee set (greataxe required)", "dharok's helm", "dharok's platebody", "dharok's platelegs",
				"dharok's greataxe");
		set("Guthan — melee set (warspear required)", "guthan's helm", "guthan's platebody", "guthan's chainskirt",
				"guthan's warspear");
		set("Karil — ranged set (crossbow required)", "karil's coif", "karil's leathertop", "karil's leatherskirt",
				"karil's crossbow");
		set("Torag — melee set (hammers required)", "torag's helm", "torag's platebody", "torag's platelegs",
				"torag's hammers");
		set("Verac — melee set (flail required)", "verac's helm", "verac's brassard", "verac's plateskirt",
				"verac's flail");
		set("Blood Moon — set + dual macuahuitl", "blood moon helm", "blood moon chestplate", "blood moon tassets",
				"dual macuahuitl");
		set("Blue Moon — magic/melee set + spear", "blue moon helm", "blue moon chestplate", "blue moon tassets",
				"blue moon spear");
		set("Eclipse Moon — ranged set + atlatl", "eclipse moon helm", "eclipse moon chestplate",
				"eclipse moon tassets", "eclipse atlatl");
		set("Void — helm, top, robe and gloves", "void melee helm", "void ranger helm", "void mage helm",
				"void knight top", "void knight robe", "void knight gloves", "elite void top", "elite void robe");
		set("Inquisitor — crush armour and mace synergy", "inquisitor's great helm", "inquisitor's hauberk",
				"inquisitor's plateskirt", "inquisitor's mace");
		set("Crystal — bow armour synergy", "crystal helm", "crystal body", "crystal legs", "crystal bow",
				"bow of faerdhinen");
		set("Justiciar — armour set (no required weapon)", "justiciar faceguard", "justiciar chestguard",
				"justiciar legguards");
		set("Obsidian — melee armour/weapon synergy", "obsidian helmet", "obsidian platebody", "obsidian platelegs",
				"toktz-xil-ak", "toktz-xil-ek", "tzhaar-ket-om", "tzhaar-ket-em", "berserker necklace");
	}

	private static void set(String label, String... names)
	{
		for (String n : names)
		{
			SETS.put(n, label);
		}
	}

	static List<String[]> readRows(String file, int columns)
	{
		List<String[]> result = new ArrayList<>();
		InputStream stream = ItemTaxonomy.class.getResourceAsStream(file);
		if (stream == null)
		{
			throw new IllegalStateException("Missing taxonomy resource: " + file);
		}
		try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream, StandardCharsets.UTF_8)))
		{
			String line;
			while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null)
			{
				if (line.isEmpty() || line.startsWith("#"))
				{
					continue;
				}
				String[] row = line.split("\t", -1);
				if (row.length != columns)
				{
					throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid taxonomy row in " + file);
				}
				result.add(row);
			}
		}
		catch (IOException e)
		{
			throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot read taxonomy: " + file, e);
		}
		return result;
	}

	static String baseName(String name)
	{
		String n = name.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT).replace('\u2019', '\'').trim();

		n = n.replaceFirst("\\s*\\([1-4]\\)$", "");
		n = n.replaceFirst("\\s+(100|75|50|25|0)$", "");
		n = n.replaceFirst("\\s*\\((?:uncharged|empty|inactive|broken|or|l)\\)$", "");
		if (n.startsWith("holy sanguinesti staff") || n.startsWith("holy scythe of vitur")
				|| n.startsWith("holy ghrazi rapier"))
		{
			n = n.substring(5);
		}
		if (n.startsWith("sanguine scythe of vitur"))
		{
			n = n.substring(9);
		}
		if (n.startsWith("twisted ancestral "))
		{
			n = n.substring(8);
		}
		if (n.startsWith("bow of faerdhinen") || n.startsWith("blade of saeldor"))
		{
			n = n.replaceFirst("\\s*\\(c\\)(?:\\s*\\([a-z]+\\))?$", "");
		}
		return n.trim();
	}

	static boolean needsRepair(String name)
	{
		return name.endsWith(" 0") || name.contains("(broken)");
	}

	static boolean needsCharge(String name)
	{
		return name.contains("(uncharged)") || name.contains("(empty)") || name.contains("(inactive)");
	}

	static String equipmentSet(String n)
	{
		return SETS.get(baseName(n));
	}

	static Set<String> groups()
	{
		Set<String> result = new TreeSet<>(SETS.values());
		result.addAll(WEAPONS.values());
		return result;
	}

	static String weaponRole(String n)
	{
		String role = WEAPONS.get(n);
		return role != null ? role : WEAPONS.get(baseName(n));
	}

	static boolean matchesAny(String name, String... expected)
	{
		for (String n : expected)
		{
			if (matches(name, n))
			{
				return true;
			}
		}
		return false;
	}

	static boolean matches(AutoCategories.Item item, String expected)
	{
		return matches(ItemVariantState.familyName(item), expected);
	}

	static boolean matchesAny(AutoCategories.Item item, String... expected)
	{
		return matchesAny(ItemVariantState.familyName(item), expected);
	}

	static boolean matches(String name, String expected)
	{
		String n = baseName(name), e = baseName(expected);
		if (n.equals(e))
		{
			return true;
		}
		switch (e)
		{
			case "god capes":
			case "imbued god cape":
				return n.matches("imbued (saradomin|guthix|zamorak) cape");
			case "blessed body":
				return n.matches("(saradomin|guthix|zamorak|armadyl|bandos|ancient) d'hide body");
			case "blessed chaps":
				return n.matches("(saradomin|guthix|zamorak|armadyl|bandos|ancient) chaps");
			case "god blessing":
				return matchesAny(n, "holy blessing", "unholy blessing", "peaceful blessing", "honourable blessing",
						"war blessing", "ancient blessing");
			case "ardougne cloak":
				return n.matches("ardougne cloak [1-4]");
			case "ancient sceptre":
				return n.matches("(?:blood|ice|smoke|shadow) ancient sceptre");
			case "mystic hat":
			case "mystic robe top":
			case "mystic robe bottom":
				return n.matches(java.util.regex.Pattern.quote(e) + " \\((?:light|dark|dusk)\\)");
			default:
				return false;
		}
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Locale;
import java.util.Map;

final class ItemVariantState
{
	private enum State
	{
		AVAILABLE, REPAIR, CHARGE, EMPTY, REDUCED, CHECK, PREPARE, CONTENTS, RESTRICTED
	}

	private static final Map<Integer, ItemVariantState> STATES = new HashMap<>();
	private static final Map<Integer, String> UNVERIFIED_IDENTITIES = new HashMap<>();
	private static final Map<Integer, String> UNAVAILABLE_IDENTITIES = new HashMap<>();
	static
	{
		for (String[] row : ItemTaxonomy.readRows("identity-review-required.tsv", 2))
		{
			UNVERIFIED_IDENTITIES.put(Integer.parseInt(row[0]), row[1]);
		}
		for (String[] row : ItemTaxonomy.readRows("item-availability.tsv", 4))
		{
			int id = Integer.parseInt(row[0]);
			if (UNAVAILABLE_IDENTITIES.put(id, row[1].toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)) != null)
			{
				throw new IllegalStateException("Duplicate availability ID: " + id);
			}
		}
		for (String[] row : ItemTaxonomy.readRows("item-variant-states.tsv", 5))
		{
			int id = Integer.parseInt(row[0]);
			if (!row[3].equals("true") && !row[3].equals("false"))
			{
				throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid variant review policy");
			}
			if (STATES.put(id,
					new ItemVariantState(row[1], State.valueOf(row[2]), Boolean.parseBoolean(row[3]), row[4])) != null)
			{
				throw new IllegalStateException("Duplicate variant ID: " + id);
			}
		}
	}
	private final String family;
	private final State state;
	private final boolean activityReview;
	private final String note;

	private ItemVariantState(String family, State state, boolean activityReview, String note)
	{
		this.family = family;
		this.state = state;
		this.activityReview = activityReview;
		this.note = note;
	}

	static String familyName(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);
		return known == null ? item.name : known.family;
	}

	static boolean needsActivityReview(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		if (identityNeedsReview(item))
		{
			return true;
		}
		if (WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(item, "restricted"))
		{
			return true;
		}
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);
		return known == null ? ItemTaxonomy.needsRepair(item.name) || ItemTaxonomy.needsCharge(item.name)
				: known.activityReview;
	}

	static boolean canPreviewEquipment(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		if (identityNeedsReview(item) || WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(item, "restricted"))
			return false;
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);
		return known != null && known.state == State.CHECK || !needsActivityReview(item);
	}

	static boolean needsActivityReview(AutoCategories.Item item, String role)
	{

		if (item.id == 30305 && role.startsWith("Special attacks"))
		{
			return false;
		}
		return needsActivityReview(item);
	}

	static boolean needsInventoryReview(AutoCategories.Item item, ActivitySetups.Setup setup)
	{

		if (setup.itemIds.contains(item.id) && inventoryOwnershipOnly(item) && !identityNeedsReview(item)
				&& !WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(item, "restricted"))
			return false;

		if (!identityNeedsReview(item)
				&& (setup.itemIds.contains(item.id) || InventoryPotionDoses.listed(setup.itemIds, item))
				&& (item.name.startsWith("blighted ") && WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(item, "restricted") || WikiCatalogue
						.entries(item).stream().anyMatch(e -> e.group.equals("Self-damaging items — deliberate use"))
						&& WikiCatalogue.entries(item).stream().filter(e -> e.facet.equals("restricted"))
								.allMatch(e -> e.group.equals("Self-damaging items — deliberate use")))
				&& !STATES.containsKey(item.id))
			return false;
		return needsActivityReview(item);
	}

	static boolean inventoryOwnershipOnly(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		ItemVariantState state = STATES.get(item.id);
		return state != null && state.family.equals(item.name)
				&& (item.id == 25781 || item.id == 13116 || item.id == 19634 || item.id == 21389)
				&& (state.state == State.CHECK || state.state == State.CONTENTS);
	}

	static String inventoryUseNote(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		if (inventoryOwnershipOnly(item))
			return "Owned guide item; its ID does not establish remaining charges, stored contents or toggle state. Check before use.";
		if (WikiCatalogue.entries(item).stream().anyMatch(e -> e.group.equals("Self-damaging items — deliberate use")))
			return "Deliberate self-damaging supply listed by this guide. Check remaining Hitpoints and use requirements.";
		if (item.name.startsWith("blighted "))
			return "Restricted-use blighted supply listed by this activity's inventory guide.";
		return "";
	}

	static boolean canRepresentOwnedEquivalent(AutoCategories.Item held, AutoCategories.Item candidate)
	{
		if (needsActivityReview(held))
			return false;
		ItemVariantState owned = STATES.get(held.id), wanted = STATES.get(candidate.id);

		if (wanted != null && wanted.family.startsWith("trident of the ") && candidate.name.contains("(e)")
				&& !held.name.contains("(e)"))
			return false;

		return owned == null || owned.state != State.REDUCED || wanted != null && wanted.state == State.REDUCED;
	}

	static boolean needsRankReview(AutoCategories.Item item, String activity, String setup)
	{
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);
		if (known == null || known.state != State.REDUCED)
			return false;

		if (known.note.startsWith("dragon"))
		{
			if (known.family.equals("infernal axe") && activity.equals("Wintertodt"))
				return false;
			if (known.family.endsWith("pickaxe") && activity.startsWith("Chambers of Xeric")
					&& setup.startsWith("Guardians"))
				return false;
			return true;
		}

		if (known.family.startsWith("celestial "))
			return !activity.equals("Tempoross");
		if (known.family.startsWith("ring of suffering"))
			return activity.equals("Zulrah") || activity.equals("Kalphite Queen");
		if (known.family.startsWith("amulet of glory"))
			return activity.equals("Mining");
		return known.family.equals("horn of plenty");
	}

	static String reviewGroup(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		if (item.name.equals(UNAVAILABLE_IDENTITIES.get(item.id)))
		{
			return "Unavailable item identity — review";
		}
		if (identityNeedsReview(item))
		{
			return "Unverified item identity — review";
		}
		if (WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(item, "restricted"))
		{
			return "Activity restrictions — review";
		}
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);
		if (known != null && known.state == State.CHECK)
		{
			return known.note.contains("charge") ? "Check charges — review" : "Check item use — review";
		}
		if (known != null && known.state == State.REDUCED)
		{
			return "Reduced function — review";
		}
		if (known != null && known.state == State.PREPARE)
		{
			return "Preparation needed — review";
		}
		if (known != null && known.state == State.CONTENTS)
		{
			return "Check contents — review";
		}
		if (known != null && known.state == State.EMPTY)
		{
			return "Empty — review";
		}
		if (known != null && known.state == State.RESTRICTED)
		{
			return "Activity restrictions — review";
		}
		return "Needs repair/charge — review";
	}

	static String annotate(String group, AutoCategories.Item item)
	{
		if (group == null)
		{
			return null;
		}
		ItemVariantState known = STATES.get(item.id);

		if (known != null && !known.note.isEmpty())
		{
			return group + " (" + known.note + ")";
		}
		return group;
	}

	static boolean identityNeedsReview(AutoCategories.Item item)
	{

		return item.name.equals(UNVERIFIED_IDENTITIES.get(item.id))
				|| item.name.equals(UNAVAILABLE_IDENTITIES.get(item.id));
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.geom.Area;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.List;

final class JoinedItemBorders
{
	private final Map<List<Rectangle>, Shape> shapes = new LinkedHashMap<List<Rectangle>, Shape>(16, 0.75f, true)
	{
		@Override
		protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<List<Rectangle>, Shape> entry)
		{
			return size() > 32;
		}
	};

	void clear()
	{
		shapes.clear();
	}

	Shape outline(List<Rectangle> regions)
	{
		Shape shape = shapes.get(regions);
		if (shape != null)
			return shape;
		List<Rectangle> key = new ArrayList<>();
		Area area = new Area();
		for (Rectangle region : regions)
			if (region != null && !region.isEmpty())
			{
				Rectangle copy = new Rectangle(region);
				key.add(copy);
				area.add(new Area(copy));
			}
		shapes.put(key, area);
		return area;
	}

	void draw(Graphics2D g, List<Rectangle> regions, Color colour)
	{
		g.setColor(colour);
		g.draw(outline(regions));
	}

	static Map<Color, List<Rectangle>> groups(List<ItemAnchors.Cell> cells, int[] highlighted,
			Map<Integer, ItemCatalogueIndex.Rank> ranks, WindowMarkersConfig config)
	{
		Set<Integer> owned = new HashSet<>();
		for (int id : highlighted)
			owned.add(id);
		Map<Color, List<Rectangle>> result = new LinkedHashMap<>();
		for (ItemAnchors.Cell cell : cells)
		{
			ItemCatalogueIndex.Rank rank = ranks.get(cell.id);
			if (rank != null && BankCleanup.isReview(rank))
				continue;
			Color colour = rank != null && config.geTierColours() && rank.tier >= 1 && rank.tier <= 3
					? TierPresentation.colour(config, rank.tier)
					: owned.contains(cell.id) ? Color.YELLOW : null;
			if (colour != null)
				result.computeIfAbsent(colour, key -> new ArrayList<>()).add(cell.grid);
		}
		return result;
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
import java.util.Map;

final class LayoutCatalog
{
	String active = "default";
	Map<String, String> names = new LinkedHashMap<>();

	LayoutCatalog()
	{
		names.put("default", "Default");
	}

	void normalize()
	{
		if (names == null)
		{
			names = new LinkedHashMap<>();
		}
		names.entrySet().removeIf(
				e -> e.getKey() == null || !e.getKey().matches("default|[a-f0-9-]{36}") || e.getValue() == null);
		names.putIfAbsent("default", "Default");
		if (!names.containsKey(active))
		{
			active = "default";
		}
	}

	String storageKey(String base)
	{
		return "default".equals(active) ? base : base + "_layout_" + active;
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.awt.Rectangle;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.Collections;
import java.util.IdentityHashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

final class LinkedMarkerRegions
{
	private final Map<Marker, Entry> entries = new IdentityHashMap<>();

	void clear()
	{
		entries.clear();
	}

	List<Rectangle> get(Marker marker, List<ItemAnchors.Cell> cells)
	{
		Entry entry = entries.get(marker);

		if (entry == null || entry.cells != cells || !Arrays.equals(entry.ids, marker.linkedItemIds))
		{
			int[] ids = marker.linkedItemIds == null ? new int[0] : marker.linkedItemIds.clone();
			entry = new Entry(cells, ids, Collections.unmodifiableList(ItemAnchors.regions(ids, cells)));
			entries.put(marker, entry);
		}
		return entry.regions;
	}

	private static final class Entry
	{
		final List<ItemAnchors.Cell> cells;
		final int[] ids;
		final List<Rectangle> regions;

		Entry(List<ItemAnchors.Cell> cells, int[] ids, List<Rectangle> regions)
		{
			this.cells = cells;
			this.ids = ids;
			this.regions = regions;
		}
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.util.*;

final class LowerTierFilter
{
	private static final String[] METALS = { "bronze", "iron", "steel", "black", "mithril", "adamant", "rune",
			"dragon" };
	private static final int[] LEVELS = { 1, 1, 6, 11, 21, 31, 41, 61 };

	static Map<Integer, String> exclusions(List<AutoCategories.Item> bank, int mining, int woodcutting, int fishing)
	{
		Map<Integer, String> result = new LinkedHashMap<>();
		tools(bank, result, "pickaxe", mining);
		tools(bank, result, "axe", woodcutting);

		return result;
	}

	private static void tools(List<AutoCategories.Item> bank, Map<Integer, String> result, String type, int skill)
	{
		AutoCategories.Item better = null;
		int best = -1;
		for (AutoCategories.Item i : bank)
		{
			int tier = tier(i.name, type);
			if (tier > best && LEVELS[tier] <= skill && usable(i.name) && !ItemVariantState.needsActivityReview(i))
			{
				best = tier;
				better = i;
			}
		}
		if (better == null)
		{
			return;
		}
		for (AutoCategories.Item i : bank)
		{
			int tier = tier(i.name, type);
			if (tier < 0 || tier >= best || !usable(i.name) || ItemVariantState.needsActivityReview(i))
			{
				continue;
			}

			if (i.name.equals("black pickaxe"))
			{
				continue;
			}

			if (WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(i, "clue") || WikiCatalogue.hasFacet(i, "quest"))
			{
				continue;
			}
			result.put(i.id, i.name + " → " + better.name + " (usable " + type + " tier; special-use items retained)");
		}
	}

	private static boolean usable(String name)
	{
		return !ItemTaxonomy.needsRepair(name) && !ItemTaxonomy.needsCharge(name);
	}

	private static int tier(String name, String type)
	{

		for (int i = 0; i < METALS.length; i++)
		{
			if (name.equals(METALS[i] + " " + type))
			{
				return i;
			}
		}
		return -1;
	}
}

package com.windowmarkers;

import java.awt.Point;
import java.awt.Rectangle;

final class Marker
{
	int x, y, width, height;
	String label;
	String category, preset;
	String guideQuery, guideContext, inventoryContext;

	String rankKey()
	{
		return (guideQuery == null ? "" : guideQuery) + "\n" + (guideContext == null ? "" : guideContext);
	}

	void clearGuide()
	{
		guideQuery = null;
		guideContext = null;
		inventoryContext = null;
	}

	Integer borderArgb;
	Integer backgroundArgb;
	WindowMarkersConfig.BorderStyle style;
	Boolean scrollWithItems;
	Integer labelArgb;
	Integer labelSize;
	String labelFont;

	enum LabelPlacement
	{
		INSIDE("Inside"), ABOVE("Above"), BELOW("Below");

		private final String label;

		LabelPlacement(String label)
		{
			this.label = label;
		}

		@Override
		public String toString()
		{
			return label;
		}
	}

	LabelPlacement labelPlacement;
	Boolean labelOnce;
	int[] linkedItemIds;

	boolean linked()
	{
		return linkedItemIds != null && linkedItemIds.length > 0;
	}

	int fontSize()
	{
		return labelSize == null ? 16 : Math.max(8, Math.min(48, labelSize));
	}

	Rectangle onScreen(Rectangle bank, Rectangle items, int scrollY)
	{
		if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(scrollWithItems))
		{
			return items == null ? null : new Rectangle(items.x + x, items.y + y - scrollY, width, height);
		}
		return onScreen(bank);
	}

	void anchorLegacy(Rectangle bank, Rectangle items)
	{
		if (scrollWithItems != null)
		{
			return;
		}
		Rectangle old = onScreen(bank);
		scrollWithItems = items.contains(old.getLocation());
		if (scrollWithItems)
		{
			x = old.x - items.x;
			y = old.y - items.y;
		}
	}

	String labelText()
	{
		return label == null ? "" : label.replaceAll("[\\p{Cntrl}]", " ").substring(0, Math.min(60, label.length()));
	}

	Marker(int x, int y, int width, int height)
	{
		this.x = x;
		this.y = y;
		this.width = width;
		this.height = height;
	}

	boolean valid()
	{
		return x >= 0 && y >= 0 && width >= 16 && height >= 16 && x <= 10000 && y <= 10000 && width <= 10000
				&& height <= 10000;
	}

	Rectangle onScreen(Rectangle bank)
	{
		return new Rectangle(bank.x + x, bank.y + y, width, height);
	}

	static Marker drag(Point start, Point end, Rectangle bank)
	{
		int ex = Math.max(bank.x, Math.min(bank.x + bank.width, end.x));
		int ey = Math.max(bank.y, Math.min(bank.y + bank.height, end.y));
		return new Marker(Math.min(start.x, ex) - bank.x, Math.min(start.y, ey) - bank.y, Math.abs(start.x - ex),
				Math.abs(start.y - ey));
	}
}

